      "evidence": {
        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Looks like a path-traversal / arbitrary-file-download (CWE-22): a FileResponse is returned for a file path built by joining UPLOAD_DIR with document.stored_filename, which a scanner flags as user-influenced filesystem access. It is actually safe: the route is ownership-checked via require_application_view(user, document.application) (403 for non-owners) before any file access; stored_filename is a server-generated value (uuid4().hex + sanitized name written at upload time, never raw user input); and the code defensively resolves the path and verifies str(file_path).startswith(str(UPLOAD_DIR.resolve())) plus file_path.exists(), raising 404 on any escape. No caller-controlled string reaches the path without sanitization and a containment check."
      },
